@marchtian — one line for hotsrm's docs, following ruling D (6380294239 above): `schedule` / `time_relative` flows run on hosted environments on the Team plan and above; the Free plan does not run them (cloud#2337 ruling C, the kernel shows "scheduled flows do not run on the Free plan — upgrade to Team or above to run them."). On a self-hosted kernel or a local `@objectstack/verify` stack, set `OS_AUTOMATION_SCHEDULED_WORK_ENABLED=true` to run them; the evaluation's `disabled by deployment policy` came from a local stack with that variable unset. Nothing changes on the platform side; the certificate-expiry sweep in hotsrm v0.1 works as designed on a paid hosted plan.

